<handout>
<title>Complicated Fractions</title>
<page>
<objectives>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            In this section we will see how to:
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <p>
                Simplify a complicated fraction by using the least common denominator.
            </p>
        </li>
    </ul>
</objectives>
<p>
   A <term>complicated fraction </term>is a larger fraction made up of smaller fractions. (To code this I had to use nested fractions.)
   <md>
    \frac{\frac{2}{x+6}}{\frac{4}{x-6}-\frac{4}{x^2-36}}
   </md>
   One method to simplify an expression like this is to multiply by the least common denominator of all of the smaller fractions. This will <q>clear</q> the denominators
   of the smaller fractions, leaving just the larger fraction which could then be further simplified.
</p>
<example>
    <statement>
        <p>
            Simplify:
            <md>
                \frac{\frac{3}{x+2}}{\frac{5}{x-2}-\frac{3}{x^2-4}}
            </md>
        </p>
    </statement>
    <answer>
        <p>
            <m>\frac{3x-6}{5x-7}</m>
        </p>
    </answer>
    <solution>
        <p>
            Start by finding the the LCD of the smaller fractions.
            <md>
                \frac{\frac{3}{x+2}}{\frac{5}{x-2}-\frac{3}{(x-2)(x+2)}}
            </md>
            The LCD is <m>(x-2)(x+2)</m>. Multiply the numerator and denominator of the larger fraction by this LCD. This is equivalent to multiplying the numerator of each 
            of the smaller fractions by the LCD.
            <md>
                \frac{\frac{3(x-2)(x+2)}{x+2}}{\frac{5(x-2)(x+2)}{x-2}-\frac{3(x-2)(x+2)}{(x-2)(x+2)}}
            </md>
            Cancel out the denominators of all of the smaller fractions.
            <md>
                \frac{3(x-2)}{5(x+2)-3}
            </md>
            Since further simplification can be done, finish by distributing.
            <md>
                \frac{3x-6}{5x-7}
            </md>
        </p>
    </solution>
</example>
</page>
<page>
<example>
    <statement>
        <p>
            Simplify:
            <md>
                \frac{\frac{4x}{x+5}+\frac{2}{x+6}}{\frac{3x}{x^2+11x+30}}
            </md>
        </p>
    </statement>
    <answer>
        <p>
            <m>\frac{3x-6}{5x-7}</m>
        </p>
    </answer>
    <solution>
        <p>
            Start by finding the the LCD of the smaller fractions.
            <md>
                \frac{\frac{4x}{x+5}+\frac{2}{x+6}}{\frac{3x}{(x+5)(x+6)}}
            </md>
            The LCD is <m>(x+5)(x+6)</m>. Multiply the numerator and denominator of the larger fraction by this LCD. This is equivalent to multiplying the numerator of each 
            of the smaller fractions by the LCD.
            <md>
                \frac{\frac{4x(x+5)(x+6)}{x+5}+\frac{2(x+5)(x+6)}{x+6}}{\frac{3x(x+5)(x+6)}{(x+5)(x+6)}}
            </md>
            Cancel out the denominators of all of the smaller fractions.
            <md>
                \frac{4x(x+6)+2(x+5)}{3x}
            </md>
            Since further simplification can be done, finish by distributing.
            <md>
                \frac{4x^2+26x12}{3x}
            </md>
        </p>
    </solution>
</example>
</page>
<page>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Try it Now!</title>
        <p>
            Simplify the following expressions completely.
        </p>
        <p workspace="3.0in">
           (a) <m>\frac{\frac{2}{x+5}}{\frac{3}{x-5}+\frac{1}{x^2-25}}</m> 
        </p>
        <p workspace="3.0in">
           (b) <m>\frac{\frac{5}{x^2-64}+\frac{3}{x+8}}{\frac{1}{x+8}+\frac{2}{x-8}}</m> 
        </p>
        <p workspace="3.0in">
           (c) <m>\frac{\frac{4}{x^2-2x-15}}{\frac{1}{x-5}+\frac{2}{x+3}}</m> 
        </p>
        <p workspace="3.0in">
           (d) <m>\frac{\frac{x}{x+5}}{4+\frac{1}{x-5}}</m> 
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</page>
</handout>